<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 54,639 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 54,639 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 54,639 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday compared to 47,737 tonnes in the same period on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Saturday    July 11</p>
<p>    Export cargo		22,657	17,545</p>
<p>    Import cargo		31,982	30,192</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Tallow		  3,020	 Trade Wind Express    12/7</p>
<p>Containers		500	 Eagle Comit	     13/7</p>
<p>Palm oil		5,800	 Wawasan Megah	   16/7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
